-- M20 §3.6: file_access_log only grows. It is the record of who looked at a KYC document, a dispute
-- evidence photo or a Park custody photo, and a record that can be rewritten is not a record — the
-- same posture M15 §2 D4 takes for compliance_access_log. Generated by appendOnly() in
-- src/db/helpers/appendOnly.ts: UPDATE and DELETE raise KT001 for everyone including the owner, and
-- komtru_app holds INSERT and SELECT only. No hand-written grants beyond these; grantRuntimeAccess()
-- finds the trigger on every later migrate run and keeps the privileges narrow.
--
-- Note what this does to the ON DELETE CASCADE from file_records: the cascaded DELETE hits the
-- trigger, so a file with access history cannot be hard-deleted at all. That is exactly D4's rule —
-- deletion is always a tombstone, because every other module holds a soft `file_ref_id` with no real
-- foreign key behind it, and a hard delete would leave every one of those references dangling.
CREATE TRIGGER komtru_append_only BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON "files"."file_access_log" FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION platform.reject_mutation();
--> statement-breakpoint
REVOKE ALL ON "files"."file_access_log" FROM komtru_app;
--> statement-breakpoint
GRANT INSERT, SELECT ON "files"."file_access_log" TO komtru_app;
